1
00:00:01,567 --> 00:00:04,533
It hasn't completely disappeared.

2
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:07,600
What's worth noting here is that,

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,180
with the development of the internet,

4
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:12,667
the media landscape has also diversified.

5
00:00:14,567 --> 00:00:16,200
What's wrong?

6
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:21,767
Miyu?

7
00:00:21,867 --> 00:00:23,267
What are you doing here?

8
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:28,567
Because of the CMS algorithm,

9
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:30,967
everyone captures different news,

10
00:00:31,067 --> 00:00:33,133
and different videos.

11
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:35,967
Naturally, their impressions vary as well.

12
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,120
"Miyu: New message received."

13
00:00:48,533 --> 00:00:49,800
Huh?

14
00:00:55,967 --> 00:00:57,267
It's nothing.

15
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:17,700
Your assignment this time is to shoot
a short film with the theme of 'love.'

16
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:18,876
- Pay attention to the lecture.
- Shut up.

17
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,500
You can work in groups or by yourselves.

18
00:01:20,533 --> 00:01:21,733
Just keep writing.

19
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:23,433
It's due in two weeks.

20
00:01:23,533 --> 00:01:25,333
- Stop messing around.
- What are you drawing?

21
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,567
In two weeks, please upload it to the usual website.

22
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,100
Hey, boss.

23
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:34,700
What is it?

24
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,143
About that time-lapse video from last time,

25
00:01:36,167 --> 00:01:38,567
I heard Hinata's last
assignment got great reviews.

26
00:01:38,667 --> 00:01:42,000
Should we ask Hinata for help this time?

27
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:43,667
Sure.

28
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:48,867
Is this the famous boyfriend?

29
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,167
Nice to meet you.

30
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:57,367
I'm Hinata's girlfriend.

31
00:02:05,233 --> 00:02:07,100
Did you have fun?

32
00:02:07,733 --> 00:02:09,800
Yeah, it was alright.

33
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:22,567
Hey, why don't you
just ask him out for real?

34
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:25,967
Haven't you been staring at
your phone and grinning lately?

35
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,767
If you really can't say it,

36
00:02:28,867 --> 00:02:30,100
do you want us to ask for you?

37
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,733
Do you?

38
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:33,667
Pay attention to the lecture.

39
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:37,900
Take it seriously.

40
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,267
I am listening.

41
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:41,009
You'll forget if you don't
write it down. Hurry up.

42
00:02:41,033 --> 00:02:42,043
You're clearly just drawing.

43
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:42,933
Huh?

44
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:44,913
What do you mean 'huh'?
You're clearly drawing.

45
00:02:56,867 --> 00:02:58,800
That's not what I meant.

46
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,000
I'm sorry.

47
00:03:11,333 --> 00:03:15,900
Hinata really is gentle.

48
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,500
Wait a minute.

49
00:03:34,767 --> 00:03:36,100
Hey, what was that just now?

50
00:03:36,367 --> 00:03:38,100
That's ridiculous, right?

51
00:03:39,467 --> 00:03:40,900
Move.

52
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:45,400
I just saw this on social media yesterday.

53
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:56,167
I've always liked Hinata.

54
00:04:15,433 --> 00:04:17,033
Good work.

55
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,767
What a shame.

56
00:04:25,133 --> 00:04:26,733
It's all over now!

57
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,567
Hinata.

58
00:04:49,167 --> 00:04:50,233
Thank you.

59
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:51,933
See you next time.

60
00:04:52,933 --> 00:04:54,200
Wait!

61
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:08,067
What is this?

62
00:05:21,233 --> 00:05:25,467
♪ My mood goes up and down every day ♪

63
00:05:25,567 --> 00:05:29,133
♪ Only time keeps slipping away ♪

64
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:32,967
♪ This love has long surpassed friendship ♪

65
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:36,133
♪ This must be love ♪

66
00:05:36,233 --> 00:05:39,367
♪ This is my love ♪

67
00:05:39,633 --> 00:05:41,700
♪ On the campus slope ♪

68
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:46,933
♪ We used to be nameless strangers ♪

69
00:05:47,033 --> 00:05:49,067
♪ The people passing by ♪

70
00:05:49,167 --> 00:05:54,200
♪ Are all running
toward different futures ♪

71
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:58,033
♪ After meeting you that summer ♪

72
00:05:58,133 --> 00:06:01,233
♪ Destiny began to turn ♪

73
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:06,967
♪ Just go for it, yet I'm
still questioning myself ♪

74
00:06:07,067 --> 00:06:07,633
♪ I can't say it out loud ♪

75
00:06:07,733 --> 00:06:11,900
♪ If this is love, it's hard to say ♪

76
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,600
♪ What kind of expression
will you show tomorrow? ♪

77
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:20,800
♪ This love is no longer just friends ♪

78
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,867
♪ This is love ♪

79
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,733
Your Sky Hare nochi Koi.

80
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:35,767
(Episode 4: "The Worst True Feelings")

81
00:06:59,133 --> 00:07:00,667
Hello.

82
00:07:02,267 --> 00:07:04,027
"Mysterious Korean
Exchange Student / DAON."

83
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,567
Hello.

84
00:07:12,233 --> 00:07:14,300
We seem to run into each other a lot.

85
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:16,367
Yeah.

86
00:07:20,033 --> 00:07:22,000
Do you like stars?

87
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:24,500
Stars?

88
00:07:27,133 --> 00:07:28,700
No.

89
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,167
I'm the moon.

90
00:07:31,567 --> 00:07:32,367
Huh?

91
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:32,933
The moon...

92
00:07:33,033 --> 00:07:34,267
(In Korean) Wait a minute.

93
00:07:39,533 --> 00:07:41,767
(Aoba University of the Arts)

94
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,133
Daon-san?

95
00:07:45,567 --> 00:07:46,700
My name is Daon.

96
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,233
In Korean, it means 'moon' and 'to come.'

97
00:07:52,467 --> 00:07:53,867
I see.

98
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:57,400
Wait a minute.

99
00:08:03,367 --> 00:08:04,867
Riku-san?

100
00:08:04,967 --> 00:08:06,433
My name is Riku.

101
00:08:13,033 --> 00:08:15,867
Actually, I like it too.

102
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,833
The moon.

103
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:21,800
How should I put it...

104
00:08:22,567 --> 00:08:24,567
Even though it's always
right in front of you,

105
00:08:25,367 --> 00:08:27,700
it always feels so out of reach.

106
00:09:27,533 --> 00:09:29,567
Whoa!

107
00:09:29,667 --> 00:09:31,167
Yay!

108
00:09:31,667 --> 00:09:32,567
Ah!

109
00:09:32,667 --> 00:09:34,267
So many bubbles!

110
00:09:34,367 --> 00:09:35,767
That's insane!

111
00:09:35,867 --> 00:09:38,367
- Awesome!
- Here it comes.

112
00:09:38,467 --> 00:09:39,000
Is everyone ready?

113
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:40,633
Alright!

114
00:09:40,733 --> 00:09:41,433
Ready...

115
00:09:41,533 --> 00:09:44,267
Cheers!

116
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,633
That's so cool, Oji-san!

117
00:09:49,733 --> 00:09:51,100
This is going to be huge gossip.

118
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:53,100
Did you guys see Sora's expression?

119
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,709
- It was ridiculous.
- Tell me about it.

120
00:09:54,733 --> 00:09:57,033
Alright, alright, calm down.

121
00:09:58,267 --> 00:10:00,267
If it were me,

122
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:03,533
I wouldn't plan such an ordinary date.

123
00:10:03,633 --> 00:10:04,500
Really?

124
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,633
At the very least,

125
00:10:05,733 --> 00:10:07,700
I'd charter a yacht

126
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:10,500
and take them for a spin around Tokyo Bay.

127
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:13,067
That sounds amazing.

128
00:10:13,167 --> 00:10:14,533
I want to go on one too.

129
00:10:15,333 --> 00:10:16,533
Then let's go right now.

130
00:10:16,733 --> 00:10:17,733
Huh?

131
00:10:18,067 --> 00:10:19,167
Let's all go together.

132
00:10:19,267 --> 00:10:21,500
Time to celebrate.

133
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:24,633
- Yay!
- Yay!

134
00:10:24,733 --> 00:10:32,733
Oji! Oji!

135
00:10:35,567 --> 00:10:37,500
I'm Hinata's girlfriend.

136
00:10:54,967 --> 00:10:56,533
What a shame.

137
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:29,833
Senpai!

138
00:11:29,933 --> 00:11:31,800
Over here, over here.

139
00:11:33,833 --> 00:11:35,933
Oh!

140
00:11:36,033 --> 00:11:37,033
Thanks!

141
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:37,900
What a treat for the eyes!

142
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,033
Shut up!

143
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,067
Did you see that?

144
00:11:41,167 --> 00:11:42,733
He even waved at me.

145
00:11:47,833 --> 00:11:48,933
Whoa!?

146
00:11:59,433 --> 00:12:00,733
Get a little closer.

147
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:07,067
The sky is so beautiful.

148
00:12:08,733 --> 00:12:10,333
I'm really so happy.

149
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:24,067
"Miyu: It was great talking to you
again today." See you around campus.

150
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,700
Not like this.

151
00:12:27,333 --> 00:12:29,033
I need to pull myself together.

152
00:12:32,033 --> 00:12:33,433
What are you doing?

153
00:12:34,633 --> 00:12:36,800
You scared me.

154
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:38,367
Are you a spy?

155
00:12:38,467 --> 00:12:41,200
I did knock, you know.

156
00:12:42,267 --> 00:12:44,567
What's wrong? Something on your mind?

157
00:12:44,633 --> 00:12:48,400
No... I'm fine.

158
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,500
Oh~.

159
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:53,200
Ah, are you texting Sora on LINE again?

160
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:56,167
No, it's not like that.

161
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,900
What is it?

162
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:02,033
Well, back in high school,

163
00:13:02,133 --> 00:13:04,667
there was a girl in my
class named Hatanaka.

164
00:13:04,767 --> 00:13:06,467
Do you remember her?

165
00:13:06,767 --> 00:13:10,300
Hatanaka, her [first] name is Miyu, right?

166
00:13:10,393 --> 00:13:13,393
The girl who passionately
confessed her feelings to you.

167
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,133
Come on.

168
00:13:15,233 --> 00:13:17,267
I didn't expect this to come up again.

169
00:13:17,367 --> 00:13:19,100
Yeah.

170
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,233
Being liked by such a cute girl,

171
00:13:21,333 --> 00:13:22,509
don't you feel anything, Hinata?

172
00:13:22,533 --> 00:13:25,000
No, not really.

173
00:13:25,767 --> 00:13:27,900
It was a long time ago.

174
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,300
What do you think I should do?

175
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,833
- No clue.
- No clue.

176
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,200
That's mean.

177
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:36,867
Because you never
explicitly rejected her, right?

178
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,933
And you never accepted her either.

179
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:45,700
That's not okay.

180
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,833
That's the most frustrating thing.

181
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,600
You know, Hinata,

182
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:54,867
you just happen to be
so indecisive sometimes.

183
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:57,600
And yet you just happen
to be inexplicably popular.

184
00:13:57,700 --> 00:13:59,867
You just said 'happen to' twice.

185
00:14:00,533 --> 00:14:01,767
What about you, Hinata?

186
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:04,000
What do you want to do?

187
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:06,767
I think...

188
00:14:09,567 --> 00:14:11,100
It's best if we just stay friends.

189
00:14:11,733 --> 00:14:14,800
Then why don't you just tell her the truth?

190
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,300
I was going to tell her that yesterday,

191
00:14:18,267 --> 00:14:20,233
but she suddenly started crying.

192
00:14:20,333 --> 00:14:23,467
And then she hugged me.

193
00:14:29,133 --> 00:14:30,600
Ah!

194
00:14:31,533 --> 00:14:32,667
What is it? What happened?

195
00:14:32,767 --> 00:14:34,333
Riku, what's wrong?

196
00:14:34,433 --> 00:14:35,433
What happened?

197
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,300
It's nothing, don't worry about it.

198
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,709
- No, that seems really suspicious.
- It's nothing.

199
00:14:38,733 --> 00:14:40,800
- Tell me, come on, tell me.
- I'll tell you later.

200
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,200
- Later?
- I'll tell you later.

201
00:14:45,033 --> 00:14:49,300
My brother might have seen that.

202
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:51,333
What?

203
00:14:51,433 --> 00:14:54,700
Nothing, I just bumped
into him on my way back.

204
00:14:55,567 --> 00:14:57,067
Isn't that good?

205
00:14:57,167 --> 00:15:01,500
Hinata is good at making those drama too.

206
00:15:02,167 --> 00:15:05,333
Besides, you guys went out
of your way to pretend to date.

207
00:15:05,433 --> 00:15:07,500
Why not just ask him for a favor?

208
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,600
Forget it, never mind.

209
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:12,033
Why?

210
00:15:14,767 --> 00:15:17,300
Maybe he doesn't even need me.

211
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:19,667
Huh?

212
00:15:30,067 --> 00:15:34,367
I've always liked Hinata.

213
00:15:35,367 --> 00:15:37,267
You know, Hinata,

214
00:15:37,367 --> 00:15:39,900
you just happen to be
so indecisive sometimes.

215
00:15:40,933 --> 00:15:44,967
My brother might have seen that.

216
00:15:46,233 --> 00:15:48,700
Maybe he doesn't even need me.

217
00:15:52,033 --> 00:15:54,533
Sorry, I need to step out for a bit.

218
00:15:54,633 --> 00:15:55,933
Hey, where are you going?

219
00:15:56,033 --> 00:15:57,167
To find Senpai.

220
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:04,767
That's so nice. What youth is all about.

221
00:16:07,933 --> 00:16:10,567
By the way, what was up with you earlier?

222
00:16:11,433 --> 00:16:13,200
You were just talking about something.

223
00:16:13,833 --> 00:16:14,900
That's so nice. What youth is all about.

224
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,500
No, no, it's not like that.

225
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,043
- Come on, tell me.
- I'll tell you later.

226
00:16:18,067 --> 00:16:19,067
Later?

227
00:16:36,367 --> 00:16:37,567
I'm sorry.

228
00:17:12,867 --> 00:17:14,300
Sorry, Miyu.

229
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,967
Can we talk for a bit?

230
00:17:16,067 --> 00:17:17,300
Huh?

231
00:17:20,533 --> 00:17:21,767
Hey!

232
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,600
Senpai, you can head back first.

233
00:17:38,533 --> 00:17:40,333
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

234
00:17:40,833 --> 00:17:43,933
What did you talk about with Senpai?

235
00:17:46,133 --> 00:17:49,600
I just talked to Senpai
about my relationship with Hinata.

236
00:17:51,367 --> 00:17:52,833
What?

237
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:58,567
What exactly are Hinata
and I to each other?

238
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:01,800
What?

239
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:08,067
I really do like Hinata.

240
00:18:12,267 --> 00:18:15,267
So, I can forgive you.

241
00:18:15,867 --> 00:18:17,433
Forgive me?

242
00:18:17,533 --> 00:18:21,167
You were just going with
the flow again, weren't you?

243
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:23,867
He confessed to you, too.

244
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,733
And you just couldn't say no, right?

245
00:18:26,833 --> 00:18:28,133
Anyway, that's how it is.

246
00:18:29,433 --> 00:18:31,400
Senpai and I...

247
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,667
This is our little secret.

248
00:18:37,767 --> 00:18:40,767
So from now on, we're a fake couple.

249
00:18:42,367 --> 00:18:43,967
I look forward to it, Hinata.

250
00:18:46,067 --> 00:18:47,733
No...

251
00:18:48,233 --> 00:18:49,467
It's nothing.

252
00:18:49,567 --> 00:18:51,900
What do you mean nothing?

253
00:19:00,633 --> 00:19:01,767
Miyu.

254
00:19:03,067 --> 00:19:04,700
I want to make things clear with you.

255
00:19:09,033 --> 00:19:11,733
When you told me how you felt,

256
00:19:11,833 --> 00:19:13,433
I was really happy.

257
00:19:15,067 --> 00:19:20,533
You're cute and really popular in class.

258
00:19:20,633 --> 00:19:21,643
Someone like me doesn't even...

259
00:19:21,667 --> 00:19:23,700
I don't need your sweet talk.

260
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:29,167
No, I'm not just sweet-talking you.

261
00:19:35,867 --> 00:19:41,333
I don't think I ever really understood...

262
00:19:41,433 --> 00:19:44,033
...what it feels like to like someone.

263
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,467
Or what it means to
truly care about someone.

264
00:19:51,567 --> 00:19:53,567
I had no idea what that felt like.

265
00:19:56,333 --> 00:20:02,133
So I figured, since you
mustered up the courage,

266
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:08,100
I couldn't say no, and I shouldn't say no.

267
00:20:11,067 --> 00:20:15,267
But in the end, I only
ended up hurting you.

268
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,300
I'm sorry.

269
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:25,433
You really thought never
saying no makes you a nice guy?

270
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:29,733
You're awful.

271
00:20:30,733 --> 00:20:33,267
Yeah... I really am awful.

272
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:43,900
Even so, I still wanted to
make things clear with you.

273
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:48,167
A little late for that, don't you think?

274
00:20:52,667 --> 00:20:54,867
It's been two years. Two whole years.

275
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:56,700
I'm sorry.

276
00:20:57,133 --> 00:20:59,033
I really don't know what to do with you.

277
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,467
I'm sorry.

278
00:21:07,567 --> 00:21:09,567
It's all my fault.

279
00:21:11,067 --> 00:21:12,700
How should I put this...

280
00:21:12,967 --> 00:21:17,833
I guess I'm just the kind of person
who can never bring himself to say 'no'.

281
00:21:18,267 --> 00:21:22,433
Yeah, I can tell just by looking at you.

282
00:21:22,533 --> 00:21:24,333
Right…

283
00:21:24,433 --> 00:21:28,333
That's why Oji Senpai
always messes with me.

284
00:21:28,433 --> 00:21:31,467
You always end up getting
the short end of the stick.

285
00:21:31,567 --> 00:21:35,433
I know, but when I'm
actually in that situation,

286
00:21:35,533 --> 00:21:37,333
I just can't say it.

287
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:41,733
Then what about today?

288
00:21:43,367 --> 00:21:45,400
I made sure to spell it out clearly.

289
00:21:46,633 --> 00:21:47,800
Is that so?

290
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:51,933
And then she called me awful.

291
00:21:54,233 --> 00:21:56,433
In a way, she's not wrong.

292
00:21:56,533 --> 00:21:58,433
Even you think so, Senpai?

293
00:22:02,167 --> 00:22:05,933
But honestly, I feel the same way.

294
00:22:07,333 --> 00:22:09,567
I was too caught up in
trying to be considerate.

295
00:22:09,667 --> 00:22:12,500
I wasn't really thinking
about anyone else's feelings.

296
00:22:16,133 --> 00:22:17,933
Well, at least you realized it yourself.

297
00:22:20,633 --> 00:22:25,067
See? You really are a sweet guy, Senpai.

298
00:22:25,167 --> 00:22:26,933
Think whatever you want.

299
00:22:30,133 --> 00:22:31,133
By the way.

300
00:22:31,233 --> 00:22:32,467
Hmm?

301
00:22:32,667 --> 00:22:35,267
What were you and
Miyu talking about earlier?

302
00:22:38,633 --> 00:22:44,133
I was just asked to check
if you two were actually dating or not.

303
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:50,433
So Oji Senpai messed with you too, huh...

304
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:55,033
It seems like he's still not planning on
giving up on Hinata.

305
00:22:57,033 --> 00:22:58,533
What about you?

306
00:22:59,967 --> 00:23:01,167
Huh?

307
00:23:01,733 --> 00:23:03,367
Oh, me?

308
00:23:08,567 --> 00:23:11,700
I think I'm good.

309
00:23:14,467 --> 00:23:15,867
After all...

310
00:23:17,433 --> 00:23:19,967
It wouldn't be right
for me to get in the way.

311
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:28,580
We were talking about something
that has nothing to do with Hinata.

312
00:23:28,633 --> 00:23:30,867
It definitely had something
to do with me, didn't it?

313
00:23:30,967 --> 00:23:31,533
Nope.

314
00:23:31,633 --> 00:23:32,700
Liar.

315
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:33,700
Nope.

316
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:34,567
Really?

317
00:23:34,667 --> 00:23:35,433
You're so annoying.

318
00:23:35,533 --> 00:23:36,400
I know it did.

319
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:37,700
Let's just head back.

320
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:39,633
Ah, you're changing the subject.

321
00:23:39,733 --> 00:23:41,067
Am not.

322
00:23:42,467 --> 00:23:45,467
I was literally stressing out
over this just a minute ago.

323
00:23:45,567 --> 00:23:46,933
You brought it on yourself.

324
00:23:47,033 --> 00:23:48,033
That's so mean!

325
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:54,533
So?

326
00:23:54,633 --> 00:23:56,433
Did you get a straight answer?

327
00:23:56,833 --> 00:23:58,900
They really are just
pretending to date, right?

328
00:24:09,300 --> 00:24:12,167
Hinata seems pretty serious about it.

329
00:24:13,033 --> 00:24:15,400
So their relationship is the real deal.

330
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:17,009
- I'll tag along.
- Why are you following me?

331
00:24:17,033 --> 00:24:18,500
You'd be better off giving up.

332
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:19,467
Why?

333
00:24:19,567 --> 00:24:21,487
- Want me to take a picture for you?
- No thanks.

334
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:23,543
- Just let me take one.
- Why do you even want to?

335
00:24:23,567 --> 00:24:25,567
- I'll do it for free.
- No.

336
00:24:25,667 --> 00:24:26,667
Why not?

337
00:24:26,767 --> 00:24:27,767
I said no.

338
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:28,567
Come on.

339
00:24:28,667 --> 00:24:29,567
I really don't need it.

340
00:24:29,667 --> 00:24:30,743
- You definitely need it.
- No way.

341
00:24:30,767 --> 00:24:32,176
- Just let me take it.
- Not happening.

342
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:33,600
- Just one picture.
- No.

343
00:24:34,433 --> 00:24:35,909
(Next Episode Preview)
I've always liked you.

344
00:24:35,933 --> 00:24:37,000
What?

345
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:39,067
A short film about love.

346
00:24:39,167 --> 00:24:41,467
Here we go. Ready,

347
00:24:41,567 --> 00:24:44,333
Because I'm the only
one who feels this way.

348
00:24:44,433 --> 00:24:46,000
Then just spit it out.

349
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:48,509
(Hinata and Sora's home date!?) Please
let me come over to your place, Senpai.

350
00:24:48,533 --> 00:24:50,267
Let's try doing a test shoot.

351
00:24:50,700 --> 00:24:52,867
So this is your place, Senpai.

352
00:24:52,967 --> 00:24:55,433
You can… do it...

353
00:24:55,533 --> 00:24:58,500
We could do something that real couples do.

354
00:25:13,233 --> 00:25:14,933
Good morning.

355
00:25:15,033 --> 00:25:17,667
- I want everyone to bond a little more.
- Right.

356
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:19,367
Let's play Look Away.

357
00:25:19,467 --> 00:25:20,600
- Look Away?
- Sounds good.

358
00:25:20,700 --> 00:25:22,043
It's the best way to break the ice.

359
00:25:22,067 --> 00:25:24,133
Rock, paper, scissors...

360
00:25:24,233 --> 00:25:25,100
Look away!

361
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:26,200
Rock, paper, scissors...

362
00:25:26,233 --> 00:25:27,233
Look away!

363
00:25:27,267 --> 00:25:28,267
Yay!

364
00:25:28,333 --> 00:25:29,233
Yes, I won!

365
00:25:29,333 --> 00:25:32,633
Rock, paper, scissors...

366
00:25:32,733 --> 00:25:33,500
Look away!

367
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:35,567
Yay!

368
00:25:35,733 --> 00:25:36,633
Next round! Next round!

369
00:25:36,733 --> 00:25:38,376
- Let's start the next round.
- Bring it on.

370
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,643
It's DXTEEN again!

371
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:42,233
Rock, paper, scissors...

372
00:25:42,333 --> 00:25:43,333
Look away!

373
00:25:43,433 --> 00:25:44,200
Look away!

374
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:45,300
Rock, paper, scissors...

375
00:25:45,367 --> 00:25:46,233
Look away!

376
00:25:46,333 --> 00:25:47,400
Rock, paper, scissors...

377
00:25:47,533 --> 00:25:48,533
Look away!

378
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:50,267
Hold on a second!

379
00:25:50,367 --> 00:25:51,709
Where are you pointing that camera?

380
00:25:51,733 --> 00:25:52,813
Let's take it from the top.

381
00:25:53,867 --> 00:25:54,867
Your Sky Hare nochi Koi

